#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wb-consistency — find contradicting rule-states before they cause damage.

Compares claims that live in more than one place (model effort caps, generated
routing-table blocks, tool references, skill descriptions vs. standing rules)
and reports drift. Read-only: never writes anything. Exit 0 = clean, exit 1 =
at least one finding.

Usage:
  wb-consistency [--quiet] [--base DIR] [--config FILE]

--base and --config exist so the test fixture can point the whole tool at a
throwaway directory instead of the real machine state (never test against
real installed presets — 2026-07-29 rule). WB_CONSISTENCY_MACHINE_ID (env)
overrides check3's machine-detection for the same reason — see
current_machine_id().
"""
